diff --git a/OPTIONS_HELP.txt b/OPTIONS_HELP.txt
index cd8fae7..dc166bc 100644
--- a/OPTIONS_HELP.txt
+++ b/OPTIONS_HELP.txt
@@ -243,6 +243,30 @@ Game controller options:
         This is two parts separated by a comma: the X and Y coordinates, as for
         --button-to-touch=.
 
+    --stick-to-pan=...
+        Use the analog stick that isn't controlling the virtual cursor to drag
+        a finger from the middle of the screen, for apps that scroll by
+        dragging. The finger moves against the stick, so pushing right drags
+        the content left and scrolls right. It is lifted and put back in the
+        middle when it nears the edge of the screen.
+
+        The value is a speed in screen widths per second. A negative value
+        reverses the direction.
+
+    --edge-scroll=...
+        With --virtual-cursor-relative=, pushing the cursor against the edge
+        of the screen drags the --stick-to-pan= finger, scrolling that way.
+
+        The value is a speed in screen widths per second. A negative value
+        reverses the direction.
+
+    --triggers-to-pinch=...
+        Use the analog triggers to pinch two fingers in the middle of the
+        screen: the right trigger spreads them apart (usually zooming in) and
+        the left trigger brings them together.
+
+        The value is a speed in screen widths per second.
+
 Graphics driver options:
     --gles1=...
         Force touchHLE to use a particular OpenGL ES 1.1 implementation.
